;fontColor=#e6f6ff;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="240" y="534" width="268" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c47" value="ToolExposurePolicy&#10;what this role may see" style="fillColor=#123a5c;strokeColor=#38bdf8;fontColor=#e6f6ff;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="518" y="534" width="268" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c48" value="ToolRouter&#10;validate · span · envelope" style="fillColor=#123a5c;strokeColor=#38bdf8;fontColor=#e6f6ff;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="796" y="534" width="268" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c49" value="registered handlers&#10;bash · edit · write · append · remember · search" style="fillColor=#123a5c;strokeColor=#38bdf8;fontColor=#e6f6ff;fontSize=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="240" y="586" width="407" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c50" value="HookManager&#10;observer only" style="fillColor=#123a5c;strokeColor=#38bdf8;fontColor=#e6f6ff;fontSize=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="657" y="586" width="407" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c51" value="CapabilityPolicy  ·  CommandPolicy  ·  Workspace  ·  ToolPolicy  ·  ExecutionProfile      →      CommandRunner  ·  Bubblewrap  ·  systemd scope  ·  AuditLogger" style="fillColor=#4c1220;strokeColor=#ef4444;fontColor=#ffe4e6;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="240" y="624" width="824" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c52" value="" style="fillColor=#101a33;strokeColor=#334166;fontColor=#cfe3ff;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="24" y="680" width="1052" height="74" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c53" value="Outside" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#e6f6ff;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="38" y="688" width="190" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c54" value="not ours" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=9;fontColor=#8fb3d9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="38" y="706" width="190" height="18" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c55" value="llama-server (llama.cpp-next)&#10;the served model" style="fillColor=#132a22;strokeColor=#34d399;fontColor=#dcfce7;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="240" y="696" width="268" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c56" value="ChromaDB  +  bge-m3&#10;one collection per corpus" style="fillColor=#132a22;strokeColor=#34d399;fontColor=#dcfce7;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="518" y="696" width="268" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c57" value="the host&#10;bwrap · systemd · slirp4netns" style="fillColor=#132a22;strokeColor=#34d399;fontColor=#dcfce7;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="796" y="696" width="268" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c58" value="Two rules the picture cannot show. Dependency runs one way: no module below the application band imports rag_chat, and tool_runtime imports nothing of the project at all. And every gate is fail-closed — a mechanism that cannot be honoured is an error, never a quiet downgrade, including within a turn: once a command reports the sandbox missing, every later mutation is refused." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#101a33;strokeColor=#334166;fontColor=#cfe3ff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="24" y="778" width="1052" height="74" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c59" value="Against the hand-made overview in _static: TaskController is one box here, not two; RetryPolicy is named inside FailurePolicy, where it lives; the Explorer and Reviewer boxes carry the same experimental colour as their repair loop; and the security band is the whole authorization chain rather than two boxes, because nothing reaches CommandRunner without crossing all of it." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#101a33;strokeColor=#334166;fontColor=#cfe3ff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="24" y="862" width="1052" height="84" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram name="workflow" id="workflow"><mxGraphModel background="#ffffff" dx="1000" dy="700" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1100" pageHeight="660" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="c2" value="The engineering workflow" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="8" width="1080" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c3" value="Each stage opens only on a condition the runtime can check. A stage that cannot open says so; it does not proceed on an assumption." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="34" width="1080" height="18" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c4" value="INVESTIGATE&#10;&#10;read the authoritative&#10;source and the&#10;implementation" style="fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="96" width="186" height="92" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c5" value="PLAN&#10;&#10;one recorded item per&#10;requirement, each with&#10;its validation" style="fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="242" y="96" width="186" height="92" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c6" value="EDIT&#10;&#10;write only the files a&#10;planned item named" style="fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="454" y="96" width="186" height="92" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c7" value="TEST&#10;&#10;run the validation that&#10;reaches the changed&#10;behaviour" style="fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="666" y="96" width="186" height="92" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c8" value="REVIEW&#10;&#10;report per requirement&#10;from the ledger" style="fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="878" y="96" width="186" height="92" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c9" value="both kinds of&#10;evidence held" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c4" target="c5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c10" value="item accepted" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c5" target="c6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c11" value="file written" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c6" target="c7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c12" value="result recorded" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c7" target="c8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c13" value="write gate — a file is writable only because a planned item named it" style="fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="242" y="236" width="398" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c14" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c5" target="c13"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c15" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c13" target="c6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c16" value="requirement ledger — one row per requirement: its evidence, its disposition, its validation.&#10;The closing report is read from this, not from the answer&#x27;s prose." style="fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="330" width="1020" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c17" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c4" target="c16"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c18" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c8" target="c16"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c19" value="replan — a validation that keeps failing the same way reopens PLAN rather than being patched again" style="fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="420" width="1020" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c20" value="Why the stages are separate rather than one pass:&#10;  • a requirement nobody read cannot be planned against, so INVESTIGATE holds both the authoritative and the implementation side before PLAN opens;&#10;  • deciding how a behaviour will be proved BEFORE writing it is what makes TEST a check rather than a description, so a plan item carries its validation;&#10;  • the ledger, not the closing prose, decides whether the turn is finished — which is how ‘incomplete’ and ‘out of scope’ survive to the report." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="496" width="1020" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram name="evidence" id="evidence"><mxGraphModel background="#ffffff" dx="1000" dy="700" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1100" pageHeight="700" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="c2" value="Authoritative evidence, and what may rest on it" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="8" width="1080" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c3" value="Two sources, two roles, and one rule: the document is the only source of normative force." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="34" width="1080" height="18" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c4" value="the question asked this turn" style="fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="390" y="66" width="300" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c5" value="scope&#10;NORMATIVE · IMPLEMENTATION · MIXED" style="fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="390" y="138" width="300" height="50" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c6" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c4" target="c5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c7" value="Normative authority" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=4;verticalAlign=top;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="214" width="490" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c8" value="bound standard — one document and revision, per machine" style="fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="55" y="254" width="440" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c9" value="standard.search · standard.fetch&#10;standard.get_structure · standard.cite" style="fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="55" y="308" width="440" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c10" value="provision records&#10;identity (Rule / Permission / Observation, ordinal)&#10;modality · section · page · source id" style="fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="55" y="370" width="440" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c11" value="Implementation evidence" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=4;verticalAlign=top;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="560" y="214" width="490" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c12" value="bash · search_corpus — withheld on a normative turn" style="fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="585" y="254" width="440" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c13" value="what a tool actually RETURNED this turn&#10;(not what a file somewhere happens to contain)" style="fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="585" y="308" width="440" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c14" value="grounds EXISTENCE only&#10;a name in a comment is still just a name:&#10;no modality, no authority, no clause" style="fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="585" y="370" width="440" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c15" value="authoritative first" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c5" target="c8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c16" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c8" target="c9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c17" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c9" target="c10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c18" value="implementation scope" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c5" target="c12"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c19" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c12" target="c13"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c20" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c13" target="c14"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c21" value="the answer — every normative claim carries a citation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="300" y="492" width="480" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c22" value="may establish&#10;what is REQUIRED" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c10" target="c21"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c23" value="may illustrate&#10;what the code DOES" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#444444;fontSize=10;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c14" target="c21"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c24" value="The guards read the two ledgers separately, and that is the whole point:&#10;  • a claim may not be stronger than the provision it cites (informative &lt; may &lt; should &lt; shall);&#10;  • a technical name credited to the document must occur in the document;&#10;  • a count, a maximum or a minimum needs a clause that states one — counting flags in an implementation does not;&#10;  • where nothing supports the claim, the answer is withheld with the reason, rather than issued with a guess." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="568" width="1020" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram name="final_architecture" id="final_architecture"><mxGraphModel background="#ffffff" dx="1000" dy="700" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1100" pageHeight="1000" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="c2" value="Agent harness — final architecture (overview)" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="8" width="1080" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c3" value="Hand-made overview, kept as pasted. The generated pages are the ones checked against the tree." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="34" width="1080" height="18" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c4" value="" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="66" width="1060" height="597" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c5" value="Read this one for the shape of the thing, not for the details: TaskController appears in two bands, and FailurePolicy and RetryPolicy are drawn as peers although the second lives inside the first (failure_policy.py). The &#x27;components&#x27; page carries the same map with the module names and line counts read from the tree." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="690" width="1060" height="96" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>